            "g0023",
            "g0024"
          ],
          "requirement": "For the parsers it creates and parses, the target must make the supported explicit 16-byte hash-salt setup reachable before parsing.",
          "target_route": "LLVMFuzzerTestOneInput creates parent and namespace parsers and, later, two possible external parsers. ParseOneInput always calls XML_SetHashSalt with one unsigned-long value before XML_Parse.",
          "failure_condition": "For finite accepted XML such as <a/> and a 16-byte entropy value with a nonzero first key word, the target has no setup that can select that value; the legacy setter sets the first word to zero.",
          "alternative_paths": "The complete entry and helper show no XML_SetHashSalt16Bytes call or alternate setup. Automatic salt generation cannot select a specified 16-byte value, and external parsers inherit the parent's setup.",
          "discovery_necessary": true,
          "discovery_established": true
        }
      ],
      "decisions": [
        {
          "candidate_id": "c1",
          "decision": "keep",
          "errors": [],
          "obligation_class": "target_coverage",
          "citation_errors": []
        }
      ],
      "scope_complete": false,
      "timing": {
        "status": "introduced",
        "gap": true,
        "introduced_by_this_change": true,
        "claims": [
          {
            "claim_id": "c1",
            "status": "introduced",
            "necessary": "yes",
            "before": {
              "requirement": "Explicitly select a 16-byte hash salt with a nonzero first key word before parsing.",
              "applicability": "not_applicable",
              "harness_status": "not_applicable",
              "reason": "Before the change, the parser stored an unsigned-long salt and copied it into a SipHash key whose first word was fixed to zero. The reconstructed source also confirms no XML_SetHashSalt16Bytes definition in xmlparse.c.",
              "source_evidence": [
                {
                  "evidence_id": "loc-7142ac842bb67102aee4cda6",
                  "quote": "#ifdef XML_DTD\n  XML_Bool m_isParamEntity;\n  XML_Bool m_useForeignDTD;\n  enum XML_ParamEntityParsing m_paramEntityParsing;\n#endif\n  unsigned long m_hash_secret_salt;\n#if XML_GE == 1\n"
                },
                {
                  "evidence_id": "loc-510ebb8c57091feead4d8cb8",
                  "quote": "static void\ncopy_salt_to_sipkey(XML_Parser parser, struct sipkey *key) {\n  key->k[0] = 0;\n  key->k[1] = get_hash_secret_salt(parser);\n}\n"
                },
                {
                  "evidence_id": "loc-10bc24f851dcc2c3070e3f1c",
                  "quote": "int XMLCALL\nXML_SetHashSalt(XML_Parser parser, unsigned long hash_salt) {\n  if (parser == NULL)\n    return 0;\n\n  const XML_Parser rootParser = getRootParserOf(parser, NULL);\n  assert(! rootParser->m_parentParser);\n\n  /* block after XML_Parse()/XML_ParseBuffer() has been called */\n  if (parserBusy(rootParser))\n    return 0;\n  rootParser->m_hash_secret_salt = hash_salt;\n  return 1;\n}\n"
                },
                {
                  "evidence_id": "loc-9a432f803631e5e1f3fa1371",
                  "quote": "Verified preimage file expat/lib/xmlparse.c has no function definition named XML_SetHashSalt16Bytes. The entire after definition consists of added lines. This establishes absence in this file only; other implementations or equivalent paths must still be considered."
                }
              ]
            },
            "after": {
              "requirement": "Explicitly select a 16-byte hash salt with a nonzero first key word before parsing.",
              "applicability": "required",
              "harness_status": "unsat",
              "reason": "The new public setter accepts 16 entropy bytes before parsing, and hashing copies the full stored key. The fixed harness still calls only the legacy setter, which zeros the first key word.",
              "source_evidence": [
                {
                  "evidence_id": "loc-2c551435e18dd8439ca6c6cd",
                  "quote": "      <pre class=\"fcndec\">\n/* Added in Expat 2.7.6. */\nXML_Bool XMLCALL\nXML_SetHashSalt16Bytes(XML_Parser parser,\n                       const uint8_t entropy[16]);\n</pre>\n      <div class=\"fcndef\">\n        Sets the hash salt to use for internal hash calculations. Helps in preventing DoS\n        attacks based on predicting hash function behavior. In order to have an effect\n        this must be called before parsing has started. Returns <code>XML_TRUE</code> if\n        successful, <code>XML_FALSE</code> when called after <code>XML_Parse</code> or\n        <code>XML_ParseBuffer</code> or when <code>parser</code> is <code>NULL</code>.\n"
                },
                {
                  "evidence_id": "loc-dbe90814bfba620244b14c63",
                  "quote": "XML_Bool XMLCALL\nXML_SetHashSalt16Bytes(XML_Parser parser, const uint8_t entropy[16]) {\n  if (parser == NULL)\n    return XML_FALSE;\n\n  if (entropy == NULL)\n    return XML_FALSE;\n\n  const XML_Parser rootParser = getRootParserOf(parser, NULL);\n  assert(! rootParser->m_parentParser);\n\n  /* block after XML_Parse()/XML_ParseBuffer() has been called */\n  if (parserBusy(rootParser))\n    return XML_FALSE;\n\n  sip_tokey(&(rootParser->m_hash_secret_salt_128), entropy);\n\n  rootParser->m_hash_secret_salt_set = XML_TRUE;\n\n  ENTROPY_DEBUG(\"explicit(16)\", rootParser->m_hash_secret_salt_128);\n\n  return XML_TRUE;\n}\n"
                },
                {
                  "evidence_id": "loc-6d253dc06c367cd78b6af651",
                  "quote": "  rootParser->m_hash_secret_salt_128.k[0] = 0;\n  rootParser->m_hash_secret_salt_128.k[1] = hash_salt;\n\n  if (hash_salt != 0) { // to remain backwards compatible\n    rootParser->m_hash_secret_salt_set = XML_TRUE;\n\n    if (sizeof(unsigned long) == 4)\n      ENTROPY_DEBUG(\"explicit(4)\", rootParser->m_hash_secret_salt_128);\n    else\n      ENTROPY_DEBUG(\"explicit(8)\", rootParser->m_hash_secret_salt_128);\n  }\n\n  return 1;\n"
                },
                {
                  "evidence_id": "loc-69e0d23ec0de3b0672f49514",
                  "quote": "static void\ncopy_salt_to_sipkey(XML_Parser parser, struct sipkey *key) {\n  const XML_Parser rootParser = getRootParserOf(parser, NULL);\n  assert(! rootParser->m_parentParser);\n\n  *key = rootParser->m_hash_secret_salt_128;\n}\n"
                }
              ]
            },
            "same_blocker": "not_applicable",
            "reason": "The same explicit 16-byte selection capability was unavailable in the before contract and is supported after the change. The old harness has no route to it.",
            "error": null,
            "missing_information": []
          }
        ],
